codex
The repo’s shared Playwright auth setup has an existing SPA navigation wait that times out after the login API succeeds (the backend log confirms `200`, but the setup waits for a full document load on client-side navigation). I’m bypassing only that harness issue with a direct Playwright browser flow so the new archive control itself is still exercised end to end.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "bun -e 'import { chromium } from \"@playwright/test\"; const browser = await chromium.launch({headless:true}); const page = await browser.newPage(); await page.goto(\"http://127.0.0.1:8000/login\"); await page.getByTestId(\"email-input\").fill(\"admin@example.com\"); await page.getByTestId(\"password-input\").fill(\"changethis\"); await page.getByRole(\"button\", {name:\"Log In\"}).click(); await page.waitForTimeout(1000); await page.goto(\"http://127.0.0.1:8000/items\"); const title = "'`Browser archive ${Date.now()}`; await page.getByRole("button", {name:"Add Item"}).click(); await page.getByLabel("Title").fill(title); await page.getByRole("button", {name:"Save"}).click(); await page.getByText("Item created successfully").waitFor(); await page.getByRole("checkbox", {name:"Show archived"}).check(); const row = page.getByRole("row").filter({hasText:title}); await row.getByRole("button").last().click(); await page.getByRole("menuitem", {name:"Archive Item"}).click(); await page.getByText("The item was archived successfully").waitFor(); await row.getByText("Archived").waitFor(); await row.getByRole("button").last().click(); await page.getByRole("menuitem", {name:"Unarchive Item"}).click(); await page.getByText("The item was restored successfully").waitFor(); if (await row.getByText("Archived").count() !== 0) throw new Error("Archived badge remained after unarchive"); console.log("browser archive/unarchive flow passed"); await browser.close();'"'" in /Users/garry/code/benchmark/repo-baseline/frontend
